dune is a beloved sci-fi epic involving  space travel giant sand worms and  high-stakes games of politics on a  galactic scale at the center of this is  one legendary family house atreides  we're here to break down this storied  clan from their mythical origins to  their strange  star-strewn legacy  it is said that the atreides clan can  trace their lineage back to the mythical  king agamemnon a major player in the  trojan war who appears in the odyssey  and the iliad agamemnon was the son of  king atreyus from which atreides is  derived this connection to legendary  kings queens and heroes is apparent in  the way the atreides family carries  themselves agamemnon led the greek  armies against troy and the atreides of  dune are similarly warlike while they  seem at first glance to maintain a  balance with nature and a healthy fear  of industrialization on the planets they  control make no mistake  their armies are still feared as fierce  and accomplished fighters they fight  often enough to have created their own  battle language a series of hand signals  to be used in conflict  just as their ancestor commanded  legendary forces in the ancient world so  too do they among the stars  by the time readers meet the atreides  family of dune they are far away from  greece house of tradies oversees kaladan  a lush planet covered in forests and  seas that is part of the galactic  patterson empire they are fair rulers  who take conservatorship of their planet  very seriously the people of kaladan are  largely satisfied and well cared for on  their planet living in harmony with  nature the atreides family is forced to  leave their homeworld behind however  when the emperor commands them to take  control of the desert planet arrakis  also known as dune this hostile planet  is a desert world where water is  punishingly scarce  humans religious refugees known as  fremen have lived on the planet for  centuries  they have adapted to the planet's harsh  surface by living underground and  building a society geared towards the  conservation of water  and when we have enough  [Music]  we shall change the face of arrakis  the pasha empire's interest in dune is  peaked by the discovery of a critical  resource the planet is the only known  source of the spice melange a fragrant  commodity found under the sand that  gives people who ingested  mild prescience  the spice as it is known is a crucial  component of religious ceremonies and  light speed navigation and its highly  addictive nature leaves the empire with  no choice but to take control of the  planet prior to the treaty's arrival the  planet was ruled by the harkonnens long  time rivals of the atreides the arkonans  are ruthless and greedy their homeworld  having been turned into a smog choked  hell in service of increasing profits  the harkonnens launch a plot with the  emperor to take down the atreides who  are wildly popular leaders that the  galactic ruler seized as a threat to his  own throne the harkonnen's time on  arrakis allows them to set traps for the  incoming family ideally in the emperor's  mind this will make the defeat of the  eutrades look like inter-house rivalry  he loans his incredibly gifted force of  soldiers and disguises them in harkonnen  uniforms  sympathetic people within the conspiracy  warned the atreides family over the trap  laid for them duke leto atreides and  many of his men are killed in the attack  but his son paul and paul's mother  jessica are able to escape  both paul and jessica have been trained  in the ways of the benny jesuit and used  their powers of observation and coercion  to survive the desert  paul is eventually taken in by a band of  fremen they are initially wary of paul  and jessica but their gifts of  prescience courtesy of the spice and  paul's unique abilities collide with  prophecies seated among the fremen by  benny jessuret missionaries  paul's goals to take back the planet  coincide with the freman's belief that  they will someday rise up and take back  control of their home as paul and  jessica learn to survive in the desert  word of paul's god-like powers spread  among the fremen and a plot is hatch to  cast out imperial forces  jessica's arrival among the fremen is  particularly well-timed she has been  trained in the ways of the beni jesuit  an order of women who secretly pull the  strings of galactic power their leaders  are known as reverend mothers and the  freman's own reverend is nearing the end  of her life the freeman believed jessica  would make a suitable replacement but to  become a reverend mother one must drink  the water of life a poison derived from  the sand worms who live on doom high  level benny jester members have such  intense control of their bodies that  they can isolate the poison inside  themselves and render it harmless  if they fail  they die if survived however the water  of life opens up a mental pathway  connecting the survivor to the memories  of all the reverend mothers who came  before her jessica is pregnant when she  undergoes the water of life ceremony as  a result her unborn daughter aaliyah  absorbs this knowledge alongside her  mother the benny jessrite know that  people born with this knowledge already  awakened before they can form  personalities of their own are uniquely  unstable they view these children as  deeply cursed abominations  jessica and paul refused to cast her out  and aaliyah becomes an incredibly  important figure in the years following  her older brother's crusade  having been shaped by their uniquely  dangerous landscape the freemen are some  of the fiercest fighters in the galaxy  paul season them a resource that can be  used to take on the emperor's  universally feared soldiers he trains  the fremen in atreides battle techniques  and the body control of the benny  jesterate creating a desert-wide army of  super soldiers together they prepare for  an attack on the planet's imperial  capital arakin  during his time outside of the empire's  reach paul also realizes the unique  power the controller of dune wields they  are the controller of spice production  the most coveted resource in the  universe necessary for travel between  planets and highly addictive to boot  whoever controls the spice controls the  entire universe thus paul uses a dual  strategy of direct attack and threat to  the production of spice to bring down  the galactic empire we must totally  destroy all spice production on arrakis  paul sets up his soldiers in the desert  outside arakin using a storm as cover  when the storm lifts they launch a  brutal assault on the capital to keep  imperial reinforcements off the planet  paul threatens to destroy the spice  something all space navigators require  to do their jobs and keep on living as  withdrawal can be fatal the emperor  concedes control to paul and he launches  a cosmic jihad to bring all known worlds  under his rule  after paul becomes the emperor the  gospel of paula tradies begins to grow  the capital of arakeen becomes a holy  city with churches and cults based  around paul and his sister aliyah  but though the empire continues to  expand  rot sets in back home  fremont veterans become disillusioned  with emperor tradies cause  terraforming has begun on dune to make  it a more habitable planet and the old  ways of water conservation are slipping  powerful forces that have been  embarrassed by paul's sudden rise  exploit this discontent and hatch a plot  against the emperor emperor atreides is  blinded by a nuclear attack on arrakis  but retains his ability to see via his  incredible gifts of prescience the  emperor's blindness further rankles his  friend followers however who expect  people who have been blinded to walk  into the desert to die rather than  burden their tribe after fathering two  children with channy paul appears to  sacrifice himself in the traditional  fashion solidifying his status as a  god-like figure among his subjects and  fremen followers alike  paul's sister aaliyah takes on the  duties of running the eutrades empire  expecting to serve as regent until  paul's children grow to adulthood  aaliyah pulls power to herself rather  than turn the throne over creating her  own cult and surrounding herself with  die hards eventually however her own  strange birth catches up with her her  unstable personality succumbs to one of  the countless other selves in her memory  and she begins to be possessed by a  treaty's enemy vladimir harkonnen when a  mystical preacher from the desert  appears believed to be her brother the  harkonnen aliyah fears her rule will be  overturned and orders his death leto ii  who has been living among the fremen  returns for his self-imposed exile and  orders alia to stand trial for crimes  against the eu treaty's empire she  breaks free of harkonnen's hold long  enough to end her own life in the  aftermath letter ii forces the  development of humanity across his  empire to suit his goal he reigns for 3  500 years before realizing that he  ultimately must die for the next stage  of humanity to develop  letter ii sets about preparing for his  death he carries on the atreides  bloodline via distant relatives despite  the fact that many of them have no idea  they're part of the legendary house he  reverses the complete terraforming of  dune returning it to the harsh desert it  once was  finally he allows himself to die in an  ambush thereby ending the atreides  empire in the chaotic period following  the death of leto ii his empire  fractures and splits into millions of  independent worlds in what becomes known  as the scattering forcing the further  evolution of humanity according to  letter ii's plan the planets that  survive indeed flourish on their own  unique terms and the galaxy continues  into infinity  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so 